Connecting to a real database (MySQL / Postgres)
In application.properties, comment out the H2 block and uncomment the MySQL or PostgreSQL block, fill in your credentials, then add the matching driver dependency in pom.xml (the commented-out blocks are already there for you).

API Reference

📋 ExecutionRecord APIs — /api
1. Get all records
bashcurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/records

2. Get all distinct dates
bashcurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/dates

3. Filter records by date — on or after
bashcurl -X GET "http://localhost:8080/api/records/filter?operator=>=&date1=04-Apr-26"

4. Filter records by date — on or before
bashcurl -X GET "http://localhost:8080/api/records/filter?operator=<=&date1=12-Apr-26"

5. Filter records by date — between
bashcurl -X GET "http://localhost:8080/api/records/filter?operator=between&date1=04-Apr-26&date2=12-Apr-26"

6. Build placeholder table
bashcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/placeholder \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "date1": "12-Apr-26",
    "date2": "04-Apr-26",
    "date3": "02-Apr-26"
  }'

📧 Email API — /api/email
7. Send performance report email
bashcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/email/send \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "toEmails": ["user1@example.com", "user2@example.com"],
    "subject": "Mozart Performance Result",
    "date1": "12-Apr-26",
    "date2": "04-Apr-26",
    "date3": "02-Apr-26",
    "label1": "Latest Run",
    "label2": "Previous Run",
    "label3": "Baseline",
    "threadPoolSize": "10",
    "jobTime": "30s",
    "sortable": "Yes"
  }'

🧪 Test/Dev APIs — /api/test
8. Get all records (raw)
bashcurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/test/rows

9. Delete a specific row (simulate missing data)
bashcurl -X DELETE "http://localhost:8080/api/test/delete?nodes=5&totalTxn=10000&date=12-Apr-26"

10. Reset — delete all records
bashcurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/test/reset